To 3D print the components for the gearbox, follow this guide. 

Step 1: Uploading the hardware 
Open the program PrusaSlicer. We used version 2.9.3. To import a component of the Gearbox into the PrusaSlicer program, first download the file of the desired component. The components can be found in the map 'Hardware'. 
Then, upload it to the prusasliser by clicking on the most left box icon on the top bar. See picture 1. It asks you to select a file that you want to add.
Select the desired component and upload it in medium quality. See picture 2. It will give a schematic overview of the component on the horizontal plane. The largest part should go on top. 
This can be done by clicking on the desired component. On the left side of the screen there are different options. Select the fourth option from above called 'place to face'. See picture 3. 
Now you can click on the side of the component that you want to face down. 

Repeat this for all the components and allign them on the board.

Step 2: Making support for the components
On the right of the screen, there is a vertical slider.
Adjusting it gives you insight in the different layers. Slide both sides up and down. If a dark blue part appears in the component, it needs support. To give this support,
there are 3 different options on the right of the screen under 'supports'. For the components that we are printing, it suffices to select support on build plate only.

Step 3: Setting up the printer
Choose the filament for the printer. Select 'Filament' on the control board of the 3D printer. 
If there is already a filament inside, first choose 'unload filament'. Remove the filament and place the new filament onto the hanger. Now select 'load filament' and put the filament in the hole of the nozzle. 
It will preheat the filament and drop the residue of the old filament. Remove this old filament. Place a smooth sheet on the bottom plate of the printer. Clean this with resin and a paper towel.
You are now ready to print. 


Step 4: Upload hardware to printer
In the top right of the screen, you see 'printer settings:', 'Filament' and 'printer'.
For print settings, choose the '0.20 mm STRUCTURAL', for the filament, choose the 'Prusa PLA - black' and for the printer, choose one of the available printers with nozzle setting 0.4 mm. 


